    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d276-a2">

                <pb facs="0789" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg575"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Señor Don Francisco Alvarado to Mr. Baxter</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>C<hi rendition="#small-caps">omayagua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-02-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 7, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to inclose to your
                    excellency the decree which has been this day issued, declaring the treaties
                    between Honduras and Salvador suspended, on account of the absolute refusal of
                    that government to fulfill the duties imposed upon it by said treaties.</p>
                <p>This step has been taken with regret, but it was necessary, as it tends to
                    maintain the rights of this country, which would suffer detriment if the
                    reciprocal obligations contracted by the two governments were only fulfilled by
                    Honduras. I do not doubt that your excellency will, with the good judgment which
                    characterizes you, regard the considerations upon which the decree is based as
                    being eminently just.</p>
                <p>I am, with the highest consideration, your, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FRANCISCO ALVARADO.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d276-a2-a1.xml" xpointer="d276-a2-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
